  "id": "Compound::DB00126 - Gene::55239",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Vitamin C and Ogfod1 through a series of molecular interactions. Vitamin C binds to P3h2, which is involved in peptidyl-proline 3-dioxygenase activity, and this activity is participated by Ogfod1. Similarly, Vitamin C binds to Egln2, which also participates in the same enzymatic activity, and this activity is participated by Ogfod1. These pathways indicate that Vitamin C may influence Ogfod1 through the regulation of peptidyl-proline 3-dioxygenase activity. The shared involvement of Ogfod1 in the activity of both P3h2 and Egln2 suggests a possible functional overlap, potentially mediated by the enzymatic activity of these proteins. The evidence supports a mechanism where Vitamin C could modulate Ogfod1 through the regulation of these peptidyl-proline dioxygenase enzymes, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
